.Dd June 13, 2026
.Dt ROMFSCTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm romfsctl
.Nd inspect and modify the N64cart ROMFS area
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm info
.Nm
.Cm free
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Fl h
.Op Ar path
.Nm
.Cm cat
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm write
.Ar path
.Ar text ...
.Nm
.Cm rm
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm mkdir
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm rmdir
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm rename
.Ar oldpath
.Ar newpath
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a diagnostic utility for the N64cart flash-backed ROMFS.
It uses
.Pa /dev/cartflash0
and the same ROMFS table/map implementation as the cartridge manager.
.Pp
The root ReBSD filesystem is not mounted from ROMFS yet.
This utility is intended to validate the flash access and ROMFS metadata path
before wiring ROMFS into the kernel pathname layer.
.Pp
The
.Cm list
command prints directory entries.
With
.Fl h
it prints human-readable file sizes.
The listing format matches the host-side
.Xr usb-romfs 1
diagnostic utility: mode, type, size, and name.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/cartflash0
.It Pa /dev/cartflash0
N64cart flash command device.
.El
